From 28ab6f303da0c6cdf6f1d8051da37c99e380506a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:38:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: rcar: set ep->desc in usbhsg_ep_enable

f_fastboot's rx_bytes_expected() reads ep->desc for the max packet size
of the last, partial OUT transfer of a download. usbhsg never set it, so
every fastboot download whose size is not a multiple of EP_BUFFER_SIZE
ended in a NULL dereference (synchronous abort, reset).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/rcar/mod_gadget.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/rcar/mod_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/rcar/mod_gadget.c
index 0e2f3089b0d..4789ee7ecce 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/rcar/mod_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/rcar/mod_gadget.c
@@ -596,6 +596,8 @@ static int usbhsg_ep_enable(struct usb_ep *ep,
 	 * nothing to do
 	 */
 	pr_dbg("++%s\n", __func__);
+	/* Function drivers read it, e.g. f_fastboot for the last OUT chunk */
+	ep->desc = desc;
 	if (uep->pipe) {
 		usbhs_pipe_clear(uep->pipe);
 		usbhs_pipe_sequence_data0(uep->pipe);
